description: Git commits must not include a Cursor trailer
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commit messages

When creating a git commit:

- Do not append a Cursor trailer, footer, or attribution. This includes `Made-with: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `cursoragent@cursor.com`, and any similar line.
- The message is only the subject and the body that explains the change.
- If a hook or tool adds that trailer, amend the unpushed commit to remove it before pushing.
